{
  "title": "Platform components",
  "uid": "platform-components",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "tags": ["platform", "components"],
  "description": "Component-native metrics for the platform tier (ADR-0501): postgres via the CNPG instance manager's built-in exporter (:9187, includes the pgbouncer poolers) and the Temporal server roles (:9090) \u2014 scraped by the otel-cluster collector and re-exported over OTLP, so Prometheus itself still scrapes nothing (ADR-0500). These are the components' REAL golden signals (transactions, task latencies) \u2014 they are not HTTP servers, so forcing them into the service-detail SLO/RED panels would be fake. Universal health for the same workloads (pods/restarts/logs/resources) lives on service-detail.",
  "links": [
    {
      "title": "\u25c0 Back to Applications",
      "type": "link",
      "url": "/d/applications/applications?${__url_time_range}",
      "icon": "external link"
    }
  ],
  "templating": {
    "list": []
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "PostgreSQL (CNPG exporter)",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Transactions/s by database",
      "description": "Commits + rollbacks per second per database \u2014 postgres's request rate.",
      "datasource": "Prometheus",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (datname) (rate(cnpg_pg_stat_database_xact_commit_total{service_name=\"postgres\"}[5m]) + rate(cnpg_pg_stat_database_xact_rollback_total{service_name=\"postgres\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{datname}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Backends by database",
      "description": "Open server connections per database. The poolers keep this low and steady (ADR-0300, transaction mode); a climb here means something is bypassing pgbouncer or leaking connections.",
      "datasource": "Prometheus",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 1
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (datname) (cnpg_backends_total{service_name=\"postgres\"})",
          "legendFormat": "{{datname}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Cache hit ratio / deadlocks",
      "description": "Shared-buffers hit ratio (left, should sit near 100%) and deadlocks per second (right, should sit at zero).",
      "datasource": "Prometheus",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 1
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "max": 1
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "deadlocks/s"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "unit",
                "value": "ops"
              },
              {
                "id": "custom.axisPlacement",
                "value": "right"
              },
              {
                "id": "max",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(rate(cnpg_pg_stat_database_blks_hit_total{service_name=\"postgres\"}[5m])) / (sum(rate(cnpg_pg_stat_database_blks_hit_total{service_name=\"postgres\"}[5m])) + sum(rate(cnpg_pg_stat_database_blks_read_total{service_name=\"postgres\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "cache hit ratio"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "sum(rate(cnpg_pg_stat_database_deadlocks_total{service_name=\"postgres\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "deadlocks/s"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "WAL write rate",
      "description": "Bytes of WAL generated per second \u2014 the write-load signal, and (with backups enabled) what ships to the object store.",
      "datasource": "Prometheus",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 9
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "Bps"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(rate(cnpg_collector_wal_bytes{service_name=\"postgres\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "WAL bytes/s"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Database size",
      "description": "On-disk size per database.",
      "datasource": "Prometheus",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 9
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "bytes"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "max by (datname) (cnpg_pg_database_size_bytes{service_name=\"postgres\"})",
          "legendFormat": "{{datname}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Longest transaction",
      "description": "Max open-transaction duration across backends. Long-running transactions block vacuum and bloat the poolers (transaction mode holds a server connection for the whole transaction).",
      "datasource": "Prometheus",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 9
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "max(cnpg_backends_max_tx_duration_seconds{service_name=\"postgres\"})",
          "legendFormat": "max tx duration"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Temporal (server metrics)",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 17
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "gRPC request rate by role",
      "description": "service_requests_total per second, split by server role (the per-role identity survives in the `type` label; the exporter's own service_name label is dropped by otel-cluster to keep the workload identity whole).",
      "datasource": "Prometheus",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 18
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (type) (rate(service_requests_total{service_name=\"temporal\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{type}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Frontend latency p50 / p95 / p99",
      "description": "Client-facing gRPC latency at the frontend role \u2014 Temporal's own \"D\" of RED. Long-poll operations are excluded: they block ~60s by design and would swamp the percentiles.",
      "datasource": "Prometheus",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 18
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.50, sum by (le) (rate(service_latency_bucket{service_name=\"temporal\",type=\"frontend\",operation!~\"PollWorkflowTaskQueue|PollActivityTaskQueue|PollNexusTaskQueue|GetWorkflowExecutionHistory\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p50"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(service_latency_bucket{service_name=\"temporal\",type=\"frontend\",operation!~\"PollWorkflowTaskQueue|PollActivityTaskQueue|PollNexusTaskQueue|GetWorkflowExecutionHistory\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p95"
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le) (rate(service_latency_bucket{service_name=\"temporal\",type=\"frontend\",operation!~\"PollWorkflowTaskQueue|PollActivityTaskQueue|PollNexusTaskQueue|GetWorkflowExecutionHistory\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p99"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Persistence requests / errors",
      "description": "Temporal's calls into its postgres store. Error rate here (right axis) is the first place database trouble surfaces.",
      "datasource": "Prometheus",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 18
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops"
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "errors/s"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "custom.axisPlacement",
                "value": "right"
              },
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "red"
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(rate(persistence_requests_total{service_name=\"temporal\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "requests/s"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "sum(rate(persistence_errors_total{service_name=\"temporal\"}[5m])) or vector(0)",
          "legendFormat": "errors/s"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Workflow completions/s",
      "description": "Successfully completed workflow executions per second.",
      "datasource": "Prometheus",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 26
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(rate(workflow_success_total{service_name=\"temporal\"}[5m])) or vector(0)",
          "legendFormat": "workflow success/s"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Task schedule-to-start p95",
      "description": "How long tasks sit in matching queues before a worker picks them up \u2014 the backlog/worker-starvation signal. Rising p95 with flat request rate means workers are under-provisioned.",
      "datasource": "Prometheus",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 26
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(task_schedule_to_start_latency_bucket{service_name=\"temporal\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p95 schedule\u2192start"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Kyverno (admission control)",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 34
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Admission review latency p50 / p95 / p99",
      "description": "kyverno_admission_review_duration_seconds. This is time the API SERVER spends waiting: every create and update in the cluster is blocked on it. The webhook timeout is 30s, and a review that reaches it is decided by the failurePolicy rather than by the policy (ADR-0104).",
      "datasource": "Prometheus",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 35
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.5, sum by (le) (rate(kyverno_admission_review_duration_seconds_bucket[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p50"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(kyverno_admission_review_duration_seconds_bucket[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p95"
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le) (rate(kyverno_admission_review_duration_seconds_bucket[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p99"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Policy results by rule",
      "description": "kyverno_policy_results_total split by policy, rule and outcome. A `fail` here is an image this platform refused to run \u2014 an unsigned build, a floating tag, or a registry that is not on the allow-list. Sustained fails mean a pipeline is producing images the cluster will not accept.",
      "datasource": "Prometheus",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 35
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (policy_name, rule_name, rule_result) (rate(kyverno_policy_results_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{policy_name}}/{{rule_name}} {{rule_result}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Controller reconciles/s",
      "description": "kyverno_controller_reconcile_total by controller. Flat zero on every controller is what the KyvernoAdmissionControllerAbsent alert fires on: a controller that is not running exports nothing, so absence \u2014 not a threshold \u2014 is the signal.",
      "datasource": "Prometheus",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 43
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (controller_name) (rate(kyverno_controller_reconcile_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{controller_name}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Admission requests/s by operation",
      "description": "kyverno_admission_requests_total. The volume the webhook is carrying; read beside the latency panel, since the two together are what decides whether the 30s timeout is anywhere near being reached.",
      "datasource": "Prometheus",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 43
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (operation) (rate(kyverno_admission_requests_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{operation}}"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
